wined3d: Support WINE_D3D_CONFIG=no_create_flags=0x800 (bug #50277)

Unity creates a separate D3D11 device with D3D11_CREATE_DEVICE_VIDEO_SUPPORT
for hardware video decoding, then shares its textures through
IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle(), which Wine doesn't implement. Failing that
device makes Unity fall back to software decoding.

Source: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11398
Applies to wine-11.0. Under Wine's license, LGPL-2.1-or-later.

